<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>GB-Link Switch LDN</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Play Pokémon FireRed and LeafGreen on the Switch with a real Game Boy Advance, or trade with the Switch straight from your browser.">
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Crect width='32' height='32' rx='7' fill='%237c8cff'/%3E%3Cpath d='M9 12h14M9 20h14M12 9l-3 3 3 3M20 17l3 3-3 3' stroke='%230b0d18' stroke-width='2.4' fill='none' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <header class="masthead">
        <div class="masthead-row">
            <h1>GB-Link Switch LDN</h1>
            <nav class="site-links" aria-label="GB-Link links">
                <a href="https://gblink.io">gblink.io</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/GB-Link/GB-Link-Switch-LDN">GitHub</a>
            </nav>
        </div>
        <p>Play Pokémon FireRed and LeafGreen on the Switch with a real Game Boy Advance, or trade with the Switch straight from this page.</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <p id="unsupported" class="notice notice-error" hidden></p>

        <nav class="paths" id="paths" role="tablist" aria-label="What links with the Switch">
            <button class="path" type="button" role="tab" id="path-gba" data-path="gba" aria-selected="true">
                <strong>GBA to Switch</strong>
                <span>A real Game Boy Advance trades and battles with the Switch.</span>
                <span class="needs">ESP32 + GB-Link required</span>
            </button>
            <button class="path" type="button" role="tab" id="path-switch" data-path="switch" aria-selected="false">
                <strong>PC to Switch</strong>
                <span>Trade with the Switch from this page: Wonder Trade, or your own .pk3 files.</span>
                <span class="needs">ESP32 required</span>
            </button>
        </nav>

        <section class="card" id="esp-card" aria-labelledby="esp-title">
            <div class="card-head">
                <span class="step">1</span>
                <div>
                    <h2 id="esp-title">ESP32 board</h2>
                    <p class="sub">Joins the Switch's wireless. ESP32-S3, C6, C3 or the original ESP32.</p>
                </div>
                <span class="dot" id="esp-dot"></span>
            </div>
            <p class="status" id="esp-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="hint" id="esp-hint"></p>
            <div class="progress" id="esp-progress" hidden><div class="bar"></div></div>
            <div class="actions" id="esp-actions">
                <button class="primary" id="esp-primary"></button>
                <button class="quiet" id="esp-secondary" hidden></button>
            </div>

            <div class="panel" id="keys-panel" hidden>
                <label class="drop" id="keys-drop">
                    <input type="file" id="keys-file" accept=".keys,.txt,text/plain">
                    <strong>Drop your <code>prod.keys</code> here</strong>
                    <span>or click to choose the file</span>
                </label>
                <p class="status" id="keys-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                <p class="fine">The Switch's wireless is encrypted with keys from the console. Four of them go from this file to the board over USB. Nothing is uploaded.</p>
            </div>

            <details class="more" id="esp-details" hidden>
                <summary>Details</summary>
                <dl class="facts">
                    <div><dt>Chip</dt><dd id="esp-chip">–</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Firmware</dt><dd id="esp-version">–</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Console</dt><dd id="esp-transport">–</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Switch’s room</dt><dd id="esp-signal">–</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </details>
            <details class="more" id="esp-more" hidden>
                <summary>More options</summary>
                <div class="actions">
                    <button id="esp-reinstall">Install the firmware again</button>
                    <button id="esp-wipe">Erase everything and install</button>
                    <button id="keys-replace">Replace the keys</button>
                    <button id="keys-erase">Erase the keys</button>
                    <button id="esp-disconnect">Disconnect</button>
                </div>
                <p class="fine">Installing again keeps the stored keys. Erasing everything does not.</p>
            </details>
        </section>

        <section class="card" id="adapter-card" data-path="gba" aria-labelledby="adapter-title">
            <div class="card-head">
                <span class="step">2</span>
                <div>
                    <h2 id="adapter-title">GB-Link adapter</h2>
                    <p class="sub">Plugs into the Game Boy Advance in place of a Wireless Adapter, with a Game Boy Color link cable. A Game Boy Advance cable does not work here.</p>
                </div>
                <span class="dot" id="adapter-dot"></span>
            </div>
            <p class="status" id="adapter-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="hint" id="adapter-hint"></p>
            <ol class="steps" id="adapter-steps" hidden>
                <li data-step="restart"><span id="adapter-step-restart">Put the adapter in update mode</span></li>
                <li data-step="choose">Let the browser use it: click the button and pick <strong>RP2 Boot</strong>
                    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" id="adapter-select">Choose “RP2 Boot”</button></div></li>
                <li data-step="write">Write the firmware
                    <div class="progress" id="adapter-progress"><div class="bar"></div></div></li>
                <li data-step="reconnect">Reconnect</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="actions" id="adapter-actions">
                <button class="primary" id="adapter-primary"></button>
                <button class="quiet" id="adapter-secondary" hidden></button>
            </div>

            <details class="more" id="adapter-details" hidden>
                <summary>Details</summary>
                <dl class="facts">
                    <div><dt>Firmware</dt><dd id="adapter-version">–</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Wireless adapter mode</dt><dd id="adapter-wireless">–</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Connected over</dt><dd id="adapter-kind">–</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </details>
            <details class="more" id="adapter-more">
                <summary>More options</summary>
                <div class="actions">
                    <button id="adapter-reinstall">Install the firmware again</button>
                    <button id="adapter-connect-serial">Connect over serial instead</button>
                    <button id="adapter-disconnect">Disconnect</button>
                </div>
                <p class="fine">Install a <code>.uf2</code> of your own: <input type="file" id="adapter-file" accept=".uf2"> <button class="quiet" id="adapter-file-clear" hidden>Back to the bundled firmware</button></p>
                <p class="status" id="adapter-file-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                <p class="fine">By hand: hold BOOTSEL while plugging the adapter in, then copy <a id="adapter-download" href="#" download>the firmware file</a> onto the <code>RPI-RP2</code> drive that appears. <button class="quiet" id="adapter-bootsel" hidden>Restart the adapter in update mode</button></p>
            </details>
        </section>

        <section class="card" id="play-card" data-path="gba" aria-labelledby="play-title">
            <div class="card-head">
                <span class="step">3</span>
                <div>
                    <h2 id="play-title">Play</h2>
                    <p class="sub">Connect the two boards with three wires, or let this page carry the link.</p>
                </div>
                <span class="dot" id="play-dot"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="session" id="session" hidden>
                <p class="headline" id="session-headline">–</p>
                <p class="hint" id="session-hint"></p>
            </div>

            <div class="choices">
                <div class="choice">
                    <h3>Standalone</h3>
                    <p>Three wires between the boards, powered from anything. This page is not needed while you play.</p>
                    <p class="fine" id="wiring">Connect the board in step 1 to see which of its pins go to the adapter's <strong>GP8</strong> and <strong>GP9</strong>.</p>
                    <table class="wires" id="wires" hidden>
                        <thead><tr><th>ESP32 board</th><th>GB-Link adapter</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td id="wire-rx"></td><td>GP8</td></tr>
                            <tr><td id="wire-tx"></td><td>GP9</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>GND</td><td>GND</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <div class="actions"><button id="wiring-check" disabled>Check the wiring</button></div>
                    <p class="status" id="wiring-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                </div>
                <div class="choice">
                    <h3>Through this computer</h3>
                    <p>Both boards on USB, this page in between. Keep the tab in view while you play.</p>
                    <div class="actions">
                        <button class="primary" id="bridge-start" disabled>Start</button>
                        <button id="bridge-stop" hidden>Stop</button>
                    </div>
                    <p class="status" id="bridge-status" aria-live="polite">Connect both boards first.</p>
                    <dl class="facts" id="bridge-facts" hidden>
                        <div><dt>To the adapter</dt><dd id="bridge-out">0 frames</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>From the adapter</dt><dd id="bridge-in">0 KB</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Board restarts followed</dt><dd id="bridge-sessions">0</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
            </div>

            <details class="more" open>
                <summary>On the consoles</summary>
                <ol class="fine">
                    <li>Switch: upstairs in a Pokémon Center, Direct Corner, Trade Center or Colosseum, become the leader.</li>
                    <li>Game Boy Advance, with the adapter on a Game Boy Color cable: pick the same thing and join the group. The Switch shows up after a few seconds.</li>
                    <li>After you leave the room, the board restarts and is ready again about ten seconds later.</li>
                </ol>
            </details>
        </section>

        <section class="card" id="trade-card" data-path="switch" aria-labelledby="trade-title">
            <div class="card-head">
                <span class="step">2</span>
                <div>
                    <h2 id="trade-title">Trade</h2>
                    <p class="sub">Trade with the Switch from this page. The board from step 1 is all it takes.</p>
                </div>
                <span class="dot" id="trade-dot"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="switcher" id="trade-source" role="group" aria-label="What to trade with">
                <button type="button" data-source="pool" aria-pressed="true">Wonder Trade</button>
                <button type="button" data-source="party" aria-pressed="false">PK3 files</button>
            </div>
            <p class="fine" id="source-note-pool">The pool picks the Pokémon you get, and what the Switch gives goes into the pool for the next person. See what is in it at <a href="https://pokemon.gblink.io/pool" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pokemon.gblink.io/pool</a>.</p>
            <p class="fine" id="source-note-party" hidden>Your own party as <code>.pk3</code> files, kept in this browser. What the Switch sends takes the place of what you gave.</p>

            <p class="status" id="trade-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="hint" id="trade-hint"></p>

            <div class="parties">
                <div class="party">
                    <h3 id="their-name">The Switch</h3>
                    <div class="slots" id="their-slots"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="party">
                    <h3 id="our-name">The pool</h3>
                    <div class="slots" id="our-slots"></div>
                    <p class="fine" id="party-note" hidden>Once you are both at the trade table, click a Pokémon to offer it. <span class="glyph">↓</span> saves one as a <code>.pk3</code> file, <span class="glyph">↑</span> replaces it; dropping a file on a slot does the same.</p>
                    <div class="answers" id="pool-answers" hidden>
                        <button class="primary" type="button" id="pool-accept" aria-pressed="false">Accept trade</button>
                        <button type="button" id="pool-cancel" aria-pressed="false">Cancel trade</button>
                    </div>
                    <p class="fine" id="pool-note">The pool's Pokémon shows up here once you are both at the trade table. <strong>Accept trade</strong> offers it, before or after you pick yours on the Switch. <strong>Cancel trade</strong> declines it. For a different one, leave the table and sit down again.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="kept" id="kept" hidden>
                <h3>Kept here</h3>
                <p class="fine">The pool did not confirm these trades, so what the Switch gave is kept here. <span class="glyph">↓</span> saves one as a <code>.pk3</code> file.</p>
                <div class="slots" id="kept-slots"></div>
            </div>

            <input type="file" id="trade-file" accept=".pk3" hidden>

            <div class="actions">
                <button class="primary" id="trade-connect">Connect</button>
                <button id="trade-decline" hidden>Cancel trade</button>
                <button class="quiet" id="trade-stop" hidden>Disconnect</button>
            </div>

            <details class="more" open>
                <summary>On the Switch</summary>
                <ol class="fine">
                    <li>Upstairs in a Pokémon Center, Direct Corner, Trade Center, become the leader.</li>
                    <li>Press Connect here, then accept the join on the Switch.</li>
                    <li>Sit down at the trade table.</li>
                    <li>CANCEL at the table takes you back to the room; sit down again for another trade. Leaving the room ends the visit.</li>
                </ol>
            </details>
            <details class="more">
                <summary>More options</summary>
                <div class="actions" id="party-options" hidden>
                    <button class="quiet" id="trade-clear">Empty the chosen slot</button>
                    <button class="quiet" id="trade-reset">Set default party</button>
                </div>
                <p class="fine" id="pool-options"><label for="pool-server">Trade pool server</label> <input type="text" id="pool-server" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"> <button class="quiet" id="pool-server-reset" hidden>Back to the usual one</button></p>
                <p class="fine" id="party-board" hidden>Keep the tab in view while you trade: a hidden tab runs too slowly for the game.</p>
                <p class="fine" id="party-fine" hidden>A Pokémon that arrives takes the slot of the one that left. Offer it again to trade it straight back.</p>
            </details>
        </section>

        <section class="card" id="log-card" aria-labelledby="log-title">
            <details>
                <summary><h2 id="log-title">Log</h2></summary>
                <div class="actions">
                    <button class="quiet" id="log-copy">Copy</button>
                    <button class="quiet" id="log-clear">Clear</button>
                </div>
                <pre id="log" tabindex="0"></pre>
            </details>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>Works in Chrome, Edge and other Chromium browsers on a computer. <a href="https://github.com/GB-Link/GB-Link-Switch-LDN">Source</a> · AGPL-3.0. Firmware is written with <a href="https://github.com/espressif/esptool-js">esptool-js</a> (Apache-2.0) and <a href="https://github.com/picoflash/picoflash">picoflash</a> (MIT). Not affiliated with Nintendo or The Pokémon Company.</p>
    </footer>

    <script type="module" src="js/app.js"></script>
    <script src="js/launcher-return.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
